From 1d607de14ecb103ef932f6ebe4d1f164824f3e88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thezerodivide <thezerodivideyt@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 12:19:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Add a target selector registry for plugins

A plugin can add an entry to every Target dropdown (gems, AAs, discs,
clickies, abilities) and supply the function that turns it into a spawn id:
core.registerTargetSelector{owner, label, side, help, resolve}. A plugin's
selectors are removed when it is disabled or reloaded.

Two related safety changes:
- An E:/F: target token that is neither built in nor registered (for
  example a plugin's selector while that plugin is not loaded) resolves to
  no target instead of falling back to the current target. Empty and legacy
  tokens keep the old fallback.
- The Target dropdowns keep a saved token that is not in the list, shown as
  "<token> (unavailable)", instead of snapping to F: Myself and saving over it.

Tests: Suite 113, plus a stub for the new call in the three plugin-manager
test environments.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
